gametitle=Grand Theft Auto: Vice City Stories (NTSC-U / CRC 4F32A11F)
comment=Definitive Edition-style controls for Grand Theft Auto: Vice City Stories.
comment=The pause menu always receives native stock controller input.
comment=Built for the original PS2 default control scheme. Changing the in-game control type can produce different results.
comment=Enable group 1 for vehicle controls and group 2 for the GTA III-style on-foot controls.
comment=Vehicle layout: L2 brake, R2 accelerate, L1 fire, R1 handbrake, Cross handbrake, Square look left, Circle look right, R3 look behind, D-pad Up vehicle sub-mission/misc, D-pad Right next station/radio.
comment=On-foot layout: R1 center camera, R2 fire, L2 aim, D-pad Left previous weapon, D-pad Right or L1 next weapon. Circle remains native/fire; D-pad Up/Down and R3 remain native.
comment=Vice City Stories uses digital acceleration/braking by default; R2/L2 move the game's digital Cross/Square driving actions to the triggers.
comment=Target: NTSC-U SLUS-21590, CRC 4F32A11F.
comment=Public credit: Zeroable.

[Cheats\1 REQUIRED - Definitive Edition vehicle controls]
description=Required vehicle controls. In vehicles: L2 brake, R2 accelerate, L1 fire, R1 or Cross handbrake, Square/Circle look left/right, R3 looks behind, D-pad Up activates the vehicle sub-mission or special action, and D-pad Right selects the next radio station. Native D-pad Left/Down are suppressed during gameplay. The pause menu always uses stock controls. On-foot controls remain stock unless group 2 is enabled.
author=Zeroable

